# Content Rules

This portfolio is a product surface, not a CV dump. Every word should earn its place.

## Voice
- Write like a senior engineer: clear, direct, credible.
- Bold/foreground text = the hook. Secondary text = proof or context.
- Use contrast: a strong claim followed by a short payoff lands harder than two loud lines.
- Metaphors are optional. Prefer plain language for enterprise readers.

## Copy Rules
- Lead with outcomes and ownership, not biography.
- Every word earns its place. If it does not pull weight, cut it.
- Short sentences hit harder than long ones.
- WIP status can use a light kitchen metaphor when it fits ("still in the oven").

## Examples

| ❌ Flat | ✅ Professional |
|--------|-----------------|
| "Check back soon." | "Still in progress." |
| "Under construction." | "Building the next release." |
| "The people behind this site." | "Contributors and collaborators." |
| "Want to contribute?" | "Open to collaborate." |
| "Coming soon." | "Shipping next." |

## Don'ts
- No em dashes (separate rule enforces this).
- No filler phrases: "Check back soon", "Coming soon", "Under construction", "I am a..."
- No film, scene, frame, or crew metaphors in code or copy.
- No humble-brag bios. Specificity > superlatives.
